    [wrong_output_shape] observe-test-behavior/pytest-skips-are-misreported-as-not-started
      `pytest_runtest_logreport` treats any skipped report as `not_started`, so a test that actually ran and skipped itself is reported as never started instead of as observed behavior.
      src/acceptance/execution/netblock.py#0
    [missing_case] observe-test-behavior/whole-run-timeout-drops-observed-tests
      If the whole-run budget expires, `_spawn_and_wait` kills the process group and `_read_report` only returns lines already flushed; any test that finished but had not yet been written is turned into `not_started`, so the run can fail to observe actual behavior for tests that did execute.
      src/acceptance/execution/sandbox.py#0
