    [scope_too_narrow] isolated-sandbox/network-block-only-python-socket-layer
      The sandbox only patches Python-level socket entry points, so code that opens network connections through a C extension or another non-patched path can still reach the network and escape the sandbox.
      src/acceptance/execution/netblock.py#0
    [scope_too_narrow] isolated-sandbox/loopback-and-unix-socket-exception
      The network block explicitly allows AF_UNIX sockets, so a test can still communicate through a local socket path instead of being fully isolated from reachable services.
