  clean-timeout-stop
    [other] clean-timeout-stop/whole-run-timeout-not-clean
      When the whole-run budget expires, the parent only sends SIGTERM/SIGKILL to the process group and then returns after a fixed grace loop; it never waits for the subprocess to actually exit or verifies that the group is gone, so the run can be reported as stopped while child processes are still executing.
