  distinguish-tried-from-never-started
    [established_not_maintained] distinguish-tried-from-never-started/completed-outcomes-can-lose-their-reason-on-flush
      A tried-but-incomplete test can be recorded with a reason in `_Reporter.note`, but later calls to `_Reporter.flush` only write whatever is still in `_pending`; if a later phase overwrites the entry with a passing result or another path clears it before flush, the original tried-but-incomplete reason is lost and the test becomes indistinguishable from one that never started.
